r('The catch is that you can\'t measure both at once: to see the bandwidth you must fill the pipe (which builds a queue and raises RTT), and to see the true RTT you must drain it.','To observe available delivery capacity the sender must offer enough data; probing beyond it can build a queue and obscure the baseline RTT. Reducing in-flight data can help refresh the RTT estimate. These are estimation challenges, not a theorem that full utilisation always requires a queue.')
